\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 10-IMF studying Argentina request for early help as peso crashes\b0\par\par\uc2 822 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2018\par 00:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Peso suffers biggest one-day slide in almost three years\par \par \uc2 * Markets fret about Argentina's ability to pay its debt next year\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  but fails to stop peso's fall\par \par \uc2 * Unions denounce fiscal belt-tightening but more cuts planned (Recasts with \uc2 IMF\uc2  response)\par \par \uc2 By Hugh Bronstein and Jorge Otaola\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Aug 29 (Reuters) - The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said it was studying a request from Argentina to speed up disbursement of a $50 billion loan program after a collapse in investor confidence in President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's government sent the peso tumbling more than 7 percent on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 It was the biggest one-day decline in the peso since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was allowed to float in December 2015. It closed at a record low of 34.10 per U.S. dollar and is down more than 45.3 percent against the greenback this year, prompting massive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nerves are frayed in Latin America's No. 3 economy as it struggles to break free from its notorious cycle of once-a-decade financial crises. The last one, which was punctuated by a 2002 debt default, tossed millions of middle-class Argentines into poverty.\par \par \uc2 The run on the peso prompted Argentina to turn to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  for the $50 billion credit line earlier this year. As part of the deal, Argentina's government pledged to speed up plans to reduce the fiscal deficit.\par \par \uc2 But given the peso's continued depreciation, which makes the country's dollar-denominated debts more expensive to pay, investors are increasingly concerned that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  help may not be enough.\par \par \uc2 "We have agreed with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  to advance all the necessary funds to guarantee compliance with the financial program next year," Macri said in a televised address on Wednesday. "This decision aims to eliminate any uncertainty."\par \par \uc2 "Over the last week we have seen new expressions of lack of confidence in the markets, specifically over our financing capacity in 2019," Macri said.\par \par \uc2 IMF Managing Director \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  responded by saying in a statement that the multi-lateral lender's staff would "reexamine the phasing of the financial program." She said that the "more adverse international market conditions" had not been "fully anticipated" when the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and Argentina reached the deal in June.\par \par \uc2 "Authorities will be working to revise the government's economic plan with a focus on better insulating Argentina from the recent shifts in global financial markets, including through stronger monetary and fiscal policies," Lagarde said.\par \par \uc2 Argentina has $24.9 billion in peso- and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated debt payments due next year, according to official data.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters after the \uc2 IMF\uc2  statement was issued, Treasury Minister \uc2 Nicolas Dujovne\uc2  said the government would reduce the size of its financing program, but did not provide specifics\par \par \uc2 UNION TO PROTEST BELT-TIGHTENING\par \par \uc2 If Macri was trying to calm investors, it did not work.\par \par \uc2 "The market is saying: 'Just the fact that you are engaging in this conversation makes me very, very nervous,'" Daniel Osorio, president of New York-based consultancy Andean Capital Advisors, said in a telephone interview.\par \par \uc2 The peso's decline has contributed to a jump in inflation, which hit a 12-month rate of 31.2 percent in July. In response, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hiked interest rates to 45 percent and sold more than $13 billion in reserves, including $300 million in an auction on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 All that, combined with the budget cuts promised to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  that will slow down public works projects, is contributing to a recession that will result in an economic contraction of 1 percent this year, according to the government. That could hurt Macri's re-election prospects in next year's presidential race.\par \par \uc2 The June signing of the \uc2 IMF\uc2  deal reduced the need for costly bond market funding and briefly steadied the peso. The government has since announced more than $2 billion in budget savings, a process Macri promised to continue.\par \par \uc2 "We will accompany the \uc2 IMF\uc2  support with all necessary fiscal efforts," said Macri, who was elected in 2015 on a free market platform after eight years of deep government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy under previous President \uc2 Cristina Fernandez\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's biggest labor group, the CGT, said on Wednesday it will call a 24-hour general strike on Sept. 25 to protest Macri's belt-tightening measures. Two smaller union groupings said they will go on a 36-hour strike on Sept. 24 to protest the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which many blame for the 2002 crisis.\par \par \uc2 "I know that these tumultuous situations generate anxiety among many of you," Macri said. "I understand this, and I want you to know I am making all decisions necessary to protect you." (Reporting by Hugh Bronstein and Jorge Otaola Additional reporting by Luc Cohen and Scott Squires; Editing by Alistair Bell and Leslie Adler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-29T23:50:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180829ee8t02c9d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
