\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The dollar exceeded $ 29 and bonds and shares were also hit\b0\par\par\uc2 1,073 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The value of the marked a new record yesterday in the local place when surpassing the $ 29 for the sale to the public (it closed to $ 29.57 in average) after brushing the $ 30 in a day in which the market seemed to want to remind the Government that the run It did not end and that the distrust towards the future of the economy is growing.\par \par \uc2 Two tests: one, the new fall of 3% that the Buenosairean Stock Exchange scored (going against the rest of the stock exchanges) to raise to 14% its losses in the week despite its recent requalification. The other, the 2.3% slippage in the bonds of the Argentine debt most operated abroad, which increased its yield to 9.5% and boosted the country risk to 613 points, its highest level in three years.\par \par \uc2 The nominal maximum for the exchange rate, which led the devaluation to 3.1% on the day and increased it to 15.8% in the month, to 42% in the two-month period and to 52.5% in the same period 2018, confirms that the peso is today the most depreciated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world. Its collapse yesterday was recorded in a day that showed the dollar stable against other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but weakened against similar ones: it fell 0.9% according to the Dollar Index, a parameter that measures it against the euro, the yen, the pound , the Canadian dollar, the Swedish krona and the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 And it was also verified at the end of a round where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the square after several days of not doing so to try to defend its value, reinforcing the usual supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the Treasury has made since it received \uc2 IMF\uc2  funds to obtain pesos to cover its deficit and, at the same time, provide liquidity to a market that came to this situation due to a marked imbalance between supply and demand of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Everything confirms that, although the change of global climate complicates, the crisis here does not stop due to domestic issues. "Argentina is being more punished than other countries and it's because of local issues," said economist and former finance minister Daniel Marx to explain the impact on the real economy.\par \par \uc2 "It's true that not only does the peso fall in. The problem is that our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls at a faster rate and does not stop accelerating," observes economist Alejandro Minteguiaga. "But in a rarefied global context, with soybeans falling and the level reached by the twin deficits of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it must be clear that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market is like paddling in dulce de leche," he says.\par \par \uc2 His colleague and consultant Alejandro Bonavita appeals to a graphic image to explain the situation: "The world lit a lighter when we were drizzled with naphtha," he says. "Given this, the only local plan is to tender the dollars provided by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , it is not enough, Argentina needs dollars and you do not see the capacity to generate them: that makes the outsiders go to dollars to go and the locals buy them because they see that the peso does not pay them and promises to pay even less, "he says, alluding to the impulse that the devaluation gives to inflation.\par \par \uc2 "This shows that the oxygenation that the Government had obtained with the changes in the BCRA did not imply a change in expectations as it seems that they expected," said CeSur economist Am\u237\'00\'EDlcar Collante.\par \par \uc2 "The government once again relied on a market that reads the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  as unenforceable for an administration that aspires to have chances in 2019. That is, investors are not believing in an adjustment that orders the accounts", explained Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Alfie , from the consultancy Radar. At the same time, Guido Lorenzo, ACM economist, corroborates that "the bullfight did not happen, it was crouched".\par \par \uc2 "You have to check recipes because theRate hike was not effective and auctions did not either. And if not, what remains to be known is what kind of change is perceived as expensive by the market: it was not the $ 25 of Sturzenegger and now it seems that that value ran above $ 30, "he continued.\par \par \uc2 The concrete thing was that the new jump of the dollar was registered in a wheel of greater movement (US $ 1017 million were operated) due to the maturity of futures, which was significant because the BCRA helped this month to expand its volume when it returned to operate ( at a loss) those instruments after almost 3 years of abstinence. That derived pesos from that spot to cash and added pressure to the dollar. "The reaction was erratic in principle, with just US $ 5 million operated, the dollar had gone up a peso, I understand that they are supporters of the flotation, but you can not let them create a problem with such a small amount that later it costs you a lot. more to disarm, "objected financial analyst Christian Buteler.\par \par \uc2 The entity decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after noon when the ticket had already taken flight: offered to sell US $ 300 million, when in the system were charged purchase positions for a similar amount. This helped the price of the ticket, which had reached a maximum of $ 29.45 at the wholesale level (came close to $ 28.10), began to converge towards the value of $ 28.9567 that arose in that auction (made after the Treasury sold the US $ 150 million it had planned at $ 29.12) and continued to go back further until the end of the day at $ 28.85.\par \par \uc2 In the BCRA they celebrated the result of this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because their idea is not to impose prices, but to dose market trends. "The problem is that the day before yesterday the biggest sale of the Treasury was read in response to a requirement of the BCRA to try to control the dollar and it was not like that: they sold more because they need more pesos for the payment of bonuses, but without breaching the parameters set in the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which proposed this mechanism since other countries had already used it successfully to finance the State in a context in which they wanted to help balance the market at the same time ", they explained in the BCRA.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180701ee71001k3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
