\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil equities slide, cenbank props up  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2018\par 17:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SAO PAULO, June 8 (Reuters) - Brazilian equities extended\par their recent slide amid political and fiscal worries on Friday,\par while the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reversed losses as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par pledged liquidity to help prop up the real.\par     Stocks on the benchmark Bovespa stock index tumbled\par across the board for a fourth straight session, as traders\par continued to fret ahead of an unpredictable October election in\par which market-friendly candidates have failed to gain traction,\par according to recent polls.\par     Recent government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo\par Brasileiro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  has also caused traders to question the\par resolve of the current government - and the ability of the next\par one - to stay on a path of pro-market policies and relative\par fiscal austerity.\par     "It's still an uncertain scenario, without a positive\par conclusion coming to light for local financial markets," said a\par Rio de Janeiro-based trader.\par     The Bovespa index was down 1.7 percent in late morning\par trade, after falling almost 3 percent earlier in the session.\par     Among the biggest losers on the index was food processor \f28 \uc2 \f2 BRF\par SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which shed some 5.4 percent, after China said it\par was slapping anti-dumping measures on Brazilian chicken.\par \par     Shares in state-run electricity company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Centrais Eletricas\par Brasileiras SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , commonly known as Eletrobras, fell\par 5.3 percent amid ongoing setbacks to a privatization program\par that now seems almost certain to be left to the next government.\par     Preferred shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2  were down 4 percent after\par analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  downgraded the state-controlled oil company to\par "neutral" from "buy," saying the "phoenix ... (had fallen) back\par down to the earth."\par     Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, jumped 3.4 percent on\par Friday, rebounding from losses of up to 3 percent on Thursday\par and 19 percent since February. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was supported by multiple statements from\par Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ilan Goldfajn\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday and\par Friday, saying that the bank would offer up to $20 billion in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps and ensure liquidity in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and interest\par rate markets.\par     In neighboring Argentina, the peso fell sharply\par against the dollar after the country signed a $50 billion\par standby financing arrangement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary\par Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 , causing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to abandon its spirited defense\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "I think (the) USD/ARS upward trend should remain intact,"\par said Win Thin, Global Head of Emerging Market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Strategy\par at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York.\par     "Once the \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  deal was reached in principle, I'm sure that\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was asked to take \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  off the table. Last\par thing the \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  wants to see is its program money burned away by\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and so the peso needs to find its equilibrium\par level somewhere north of 25."\par     The Argentine peso was down 2 percent at 25.5 per dollar in\par midday trade while the Mexican peso was down 0.4 percent at\par 20.56 per dollar.\par     \par Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1454 GMT:  \par     \par  Stock indexes             Latest          Daily   YTD pct\par                                              pct    change\par                                           change  \par  MSCI Emerging Markets        1,133.26     -1.43     -0.76\par                                                   \par  MSCI LatAm                   2,452.36      0.12    -13.39\par                                                   \par  Brazil Bovespa              72,627.80     -1.66     -4.94\par  Mexico IPC                  45,457.48     -0.04     -7.90\par  Chile IPSA                   5,457.46     -0.19     -1.93\par  Chile IGPA                  27,646.18     -0.08     -1.20\par  Argentina MerVal            30,852.93      2.24      2.62\par  Colombia IGBC               12,251.93     -0.09      7.75\par  Venezuela IBC               40,372.64      1.28  3,096.21\par                                                           \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest     Daily   YTD pct\par                                              pct    change\par                                           change  \par  Brazil real                    3.7933      3.42    -12.65\par  Mexico peso                   20.5645     -0.39     -4.21\par  Chile peso                      630.8     -0