\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 ARGENTINA: Merval Climbs 4.55% On Expectations Of Agreement With \uc2 IMF\b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Merval, the main index of the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange, rose 4.55% to 30,359.26 points Tuesday, mainly driven by the shares of banks and energy companies. The good mood in the market is also related to the growing expectation for the signing of the agreement between Mauricio Macri's administration and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 )."Although the figures have not yet been disclosed, the market is betting that Argentina could have access to a standby credit higher than the estimate," said Eduardo Fernandez, an analyst at Rava Bursatil.IMF's director for the Western Hemisphere Department, \uc2 Alejandro Werner\uc2 , said that "the negotiations are well advanced."The expectations are for the agreement to be signed in the coming days.The shares of Banco Francis (+11.76%), Distribuidora de Gas Cuyana (+9.41%), and Supervielle (+8.21%) rose sharply. The only company to close lower was \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (-3.80%).Meanwhile, the locally traded U.S.\par \par \uc2  dollar closed with a subtle drop of 0.04%, at 24.96 Argentinean pesos, with the Banco de la Nacien selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid the USD rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, avoiding \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA). The U.S. dollar keeps on rising amid expectations of an agreement between Argentina and the \uc2 IMF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180605ee650059j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picsc