\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The US 10-year bonds they reach their highest rate since 2011\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The 10-year US debt on Tuesday reached its best performance since 2011 reflecting the fear of rising inflation and interest rates of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed). >> The 10-year \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  yield, a key benchmark for markets, surpassed 3.05% by 12H50 GMT for the first time since July 2011 and continued to rise to 3.09%. >> This increase strengthened the dollar against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One of the exceptions was \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  where, thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso appreciated 3.61% after having lost more than 6% on Monday in the middle of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange that has depreciated its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 12.63%. that goes of the month. >> The rise in bonds also affected Wall Street, which closed down. >> "This is the first time that the increase in rates seems to have a significant impact on stock market indices, and investors seem to be looking more and more towards Treasury bonds," said Karl Haeling of LBBW.\par \par \uc2  >> Analysts estimate that 10-year bond rates will continue to rise and some believe they will surpass 3.5%. These increases can cause investors to exit the stock market and bet on bonds that are safer assets and with increasing returns. >> The biggest gain offered by the bonds "reflects the expectations of increases in the regular rates of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Fed) due to a rise in inflation and the improvement in the outlook for economic growth in the second quarter," Karl commented. Haeling vice president of the LBBW bank. >> This Tuesday the publication of positive economic indicators on retail sales in April and the manufacturing activity of the New York region, pushed up the rates, observed analysts at the financial corporation \uc2 Charles Schwab\uc2 . >> Four rate increases & nbsp;>> The consumer price index released last Thursday showed a rise of 2.5% in one year and 2.1% if volatile values ??such as food and energy are excluded. Those levels are quite close to the inflation target of 2% of the Fed.>> Inflation was also fueled by the increase in oil prices. In New York the barrel has gained 6% so far this month. >> "The novelty for several days now is that brokers are betting that there is more than 50% chance that the Fed will increase rates four times this year and not three," said Nicholas Colas of analyst firm DataTrek. "It's a change that seems bland but very important," he said. >> The performance of US Treasuries evolves in parallel with the Fed's increases.>> "The best view of the market is for the Fed. If it worries about the advance of inflation, to the point of imposing a quarter increase in rates, then the bond market worries. " He said. >> The current tension observed in US interest rates is also a result of the increase in the government's debt issuance targets. >> "To pour more Treasury bonds in the market, the administration should offer more" paper yields, said Colas, who estimated that the market should get used to it because it is expected to issue more debt in the coming years. >\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180516ee5g002tb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
