\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Hundreds of Argentines protest against \uc2 IMF\uc2  rescue\b0\par\par\uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Several hundred people marched this Monday in the center of Buenos Aires against the "tarifazo & # 39; in public services and that the Argentine government go to the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) in a day in which the dollar exceeded 25 pesos for sale. With phrases like "the worst is over, but the terrible is yet to come" or "we're going up, fuck, the change is coming", several demonstrators satirized the messages of the Executive, which calls for calm amid an unstoppable rise in prices of public services while the peso devalues ??and wages remain practically frozen. In view of this situation, Juan Carlos Schmid, one of the three secretaries of the General Confederation of Labor (CGT), presented his rejection of "the rate schedule", "the return to international financial organizations" and "absolutely nothing to discuss the agreements and on labor legislation ".\par \par \uc2  We recommend: The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  performs a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "No one can pay the tariff chart that has been launched," said Schmid, microphone in hand, at the foot of the iconic Obelisk. Since coming to power in December 2015, Macri has insisted on the need to update electricity or gas tariffs after years of stagnation due to being heavily subsidized during the Government of \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  (2007-2015), which according to the Current executive caused a strong disinvestment in the energy sector. The protest on Monday also had the presence of the Argentine Confederation of Transport Workers (CATT) and the National Union Youth (JSN), the Argentine Aircraft Association or the Textile Workers Association (AOTRA), among others. Lee: \uc2 IMF\uc2  support for Argentina is bad news, says former finance minister In this line, the Secretary General of the AOTRA, Hugo Ben\u237\'00\'EDtez, told Efe that he has the "hope" that the Executive "will listen to the workers' demand and that it will really open a dialogue table" in which the unions are included. , opposition and civil associations. "We are still in time for the government to listen to our claims and call us to try to see how we come out of this crisis together that really is tormenting us and a lot," he said. Under a shower of counterfeit bills of 5,000 pesos (about 200 dollars) with the face of the Minister of Mining and Energy, \uc2 Juan Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Aranguren\uc2 , spoke to Efe Juan Pablo Brey, Secretary General of Aeronavegantes and youth secretary of the CGT, who denounced that "There are workers who have had to take credit to pay for these essential services (water, electricity and gas) for any human being." For this reason, he supported the announcement made this morning by Schmid, who assured that there will be a national strike if the Government's measures continue in this line while asking patience to have the support of all citizens. We recommend: How does the stand-by agreement that Argentina asks the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ? "We have to organize it, we have to work on it, we are all convinced of the diagnosis we have, we are all convinced of where this government is going and where we do not want to go, but unemployment must be worked on," said Brey in support of the triumvirate. Since April 25, the Argentine peso has been abruptly devalued due to the sharp rise in rates in the United States and the consequent flight of capital to that country, which has strongly upset the Argentine political, economic and social sector and has forced the Government to start negotiating credits with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and other multilateral organizations to mitigate the consequences This Monday, the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again fell sharply: 7.59% against the dollar in the openingof markets.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180515ee5f000rf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
