\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentine peso is heading into the worst week since 2015\b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso was heading towards its worst week since December 2015 after the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said it wants to conclude talks on a possible line of credit as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 The peso fell 3.9% to 23.6 per dollar at 1:44 pm in Buenos Aires, extending the weekly drop to 7.6%. Previously, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars and bought letters from the short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Lebacs, to stop the fall of the peso to a record of 24.1 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 , managing director of the International Monetary Fund, said on Thursday that the bank is looking for a quick solution to the talks with Argentina on the establishment of a right-of-way agreement. That did little to calm the world's worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. The peso fell 6.5% at a time before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which did little to calm the nervousness.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would be requesting a line of credit for up to US $ 30,000 million, will resume talks with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  next week. The government is also in talks with the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 , the \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  and the Latin American Development Bank (CAF) for additional lines of credit, Finance Minister Luis Caputo said Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will face its first big test at Tuesday's auction of Lebacs, where around US $ 30 billion of bills must be renewed before they expire on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also stopped adding liquidity to the markets through its inverse repo of up to 47%, according to a person with knowledge of the subject. By stopping the inverse repo the additional entry of weights to the market is stopped, which prevents operators from using those pesos to buy dollars. The center of the bank's 7-day repo range of 40% is used as the monetary policy rate.\par \par \uc2 The Argentine Peso entry is heading towards the worst week since 2015 was first published in La Tercera.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180511ee5b00444\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
