\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s Move to Seek IMF Aid Fails to Halt Market Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2018\par 20:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s announcement Tuesday that it is seeking a line of credit from the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  failed to stem the more than weeklong slide in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stocks and bonds as foreign investors continued to flee the troubled market.\par \par \uc2 The appeal to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  for help follows three unannounced emergency interest-rate hikes by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s benchmark interest rate reached 40% last week following the increases, briefly pausing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s slide.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI Argentina index was down 6% recently, retracing from steeper losses in early morning trading that at one point had the widely tracked equities benchmark down as much as 8% on the day. The Argentine peso weakened against the dollar, which was up 2%. \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s benchmark Argentine bond index fell slightly, reaching its lowest level in more than a year.\par \par \uc2 Argentine equities have \u8203\'20\'0Bdropped 19% this month and are down 29% so far this year. The Argentine peso has weakened 10% against the dollar since the government began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the end of last month.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a history of fiscal mismanagement, government debt defaults and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation. The new administration under President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  has worked hard to win back foreign investors and encourage bank lending with more pro-business policies, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered interest rates at the start of the year in an attempt to stimulate growth.\par \par \uc2 But the plan backfired as foreign investors questioned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s independence and began selling the country\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a long, tough road to regain and fully restore policy credibility, much of which was unnecessarily damaged,\u8221\'20\'1D said Patrick Esteruelas, head of research at Emso Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 Still, not everyone is bracing for another Argentine crisis. UBS Global Wealth Management\u8217\'20\'19s chief investment office said that while Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s soaring inflation and interest rates will undermine growth, it is unlikely to lead to a recession. Borrowing in Argentina had only recently begun to take off. While bank lending grew 25% in real terms last year, debt levels in Argentina remain the lowest in Latin America, at about 16% of gross domestic product 2017. That is expected to rise to 20% of GDP this year, says Charles Robertson, global chief economist at investment bank Renaissance Capital.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArgentinians don\u8217\'20\'19t borrow money; so, most people shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t care about interest rates going to very high levels,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd inflation is not as important if you don\u8217\'20\'19t have savings in your local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A big chunk of Argentinian savings have been kept offshore in Uruguay for many years because they are wary of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mr. Robertson said the recent slide doesn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily portend another crisis for Argentina, which hasn\u8217\'20\'19t resorted to capital controls as it did in the past or seen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drop below the firm\u8217\'20\'19s estimated fair value for the peso.\par \par \uc2 Write to Julie Wernau at Julie.Wernau@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 08, 2018 14:50 ET (18:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180508ee58003e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
