\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Argentina peso tumbles again despite cenbank moves\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2018\par 23:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices; adds news from Brazil and Mexico)\par     By Gram Slattery\par     SAO PAULO, May 3 (Reuters) - The Argentine peso hit a new\par record low on Thursday, dropping for the second straight day\par despite a dramatic rate hike by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , indicating\par investors are jittery about a market-friendly transition in\par Argentina.\par     In afternoon trading, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell nearly 8\par percent to trade at 23 pesos per U.S. dollar, even as the bank\par hiked the benchmark interest rate 300 basis points to 33.25\par percent, its second surprise hike in less than a week.\par \par     The bank said in a Thursday statement it would continue\par using all the tools at its disposal to achieve its 15 percent\par inflation target this year and could raise the interest rate\par again.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also heavily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in the spot market, selling about $500 million on Thursday,\par according to traders, after selling the same amount the day\par before.\par     Elsewhere in the region, other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mainly flat\par against the dollar, though Colombia's peso was off 0.88\par percent as prices for oil took a slide.\par     Regional equities markets were all down as trade jitters\par weighed on sentiment ahead of a U.S. trade visit to China, with\par Brazil's benchmark Bovespa and Mexico's S&P/BMV IPC index both\par down about 1.5 percent.\par     Shares in Brazil's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco BTG Pactual\f28 \uc2 \f2  tumbled 2\par percent on Thursday, the day after the country's largest\par independent investment bank reported profits fell more than 20\par percent in the latest quarter.\par     In Mexico, shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kimberly-Clark de Mexico\f28 \uc2 \f2  dropped as\par much as 6.5 percent to trade at its lowest since April 2015.\par \par     U.S. Treasury Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Steven Mnuchin\f28 \uc2 \f2  has arrived in\par Beijing for talks on tariffs, but with state media saying China\par will stand up to the United States and the U.S. delegation\par slated to leave as early as Friday, there is little expectation\par of a breakthrough.\par \par Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2034 GMT:    \par     \par  Stock indexes                Latest   Daily pct   YTD pct\par                                           change    change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets       1,137.85      -1.18     -1.78\par                                                   \par  MSCI LatAm                  2,841.05      -1.85      0.46\par                                                   \par  Brazil Bovespa             83,288.14      -1.49      9.01\par  Mexico IPC                 47,094.13       -1.5     -4.58\par  Chile IPSA                  5,640.10      -0.96      1.36\par  Chile IGPA                 28,413.30      -0.82      1.55\par                                                   \par  Argentina MerVal           29,567.99      -0.16     -1.66\par  Colombia IGBC              12,353.29      -0.59      8.64\par  Venezuela IBC              21,977.18       1.23   1639.88\par                                                           \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                    Latest   Daily pct   YTD pct\par                                        