\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stress levels rise as Argentina peso, Turkish lira hit record lows\b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2018\par 10:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Turkish lira hits record low after jump in inflation\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall to halt \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso plunge\par \par \uc2 * Stocks fall for third day towards three-month low\par \par \uc2 * CEE digest \uc2 EU\uc2  budget plans, \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold rates\par \par \uc2 By Marc Jones\par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 3 (Reuters) - Stress levels rose in emerging markets on Thursday as Argentina's peso and Turkey's lira slumped to record lows in what looked like classic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attacks and shares fell for a third day.\par \par \uc2 The pressure was widespread against the backdrop of a rising dollar and global borrowing rates and after more unpredictable behaviour on metal export tariffs from U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's administration towards Brazil overnight.\par \par \uc2 It combined to push MSCI's 24-country emerging market stocks index towards a three-month low though tensions were highest in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's peso slumped over 3 percent to an all-time low of 21.2 per dollar despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  just days after an emergency interest rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Turkey then saw the lira slide 0.4 percent to an all-time trough of 4.21 to the dollar, as another jump in inflation there added to jitters caused by a rating downgrade this week and government plans to up spending.\par \par \uc2 "You have this vicious circle of a deteriorating inflation outlook, a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is behind the curve," said ING's Chief EMEA \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate strategist, Petr Krpata.\par \par \uc2 Pressure also remained on the Central and Eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that were some of last year's best performers in the world.\par \par \uc2 The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to keep its rates steady at a meeting later but the slide in the crown against both the dollar and the euro has boosted chances of another hike later in the year, Krpata added.\par \par \uc2 The region was also digesting news that from 2021 the \uc2 European Union\uc2  will cut funds paid out to member states that undermine courts and the rule of law, a move that could cost Hungary and Poland millions of euros.\par \par \uc2 Eurosceptic nationalists who have come to power in some former Communist states of eastern Europe have clashed with Brussels over what the \uc2 EU\uc2  describes as curbs to freedom of the media and violations of other democratic norms.\par \par \uc2 In Asia overnight, Indonesia's rupiah had fallen to its lowest in more than two years as foreign investors continued to sell their positions in the local bond and equity markets.\par \par \uc2 Indonesian stock exchange and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed foreigners sold securities worth $684 million in equity markets and $967 million in bonds in April.\par \par \uc2 It was not all one way traffic however. The Singapore dollar and the Thai baht rose 0.25 percent and 0.15 percent respectively. The Indian rupee and the South Korean won also edged up on the day, the latter buoyed by an ongoing improvement of relations with North Korea.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America though there had been more gloomy news for turmoil-ridden Venezuela as the \uc2 IMF\uc2  issued a "declaration of censure" against Venezuela for failing to provide necessary economic data.\par \par \uc2 The United States cut off metals tariff talks with Brazil, contradicting an earlier U.S. announcement that the two countries had reached a permanent exemption from steel and aluminium import tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for Brazil's industry decried U.S. negotiation tactics, which the head of the association for aluminium producers, Milton Rego, called "Al Capone-like."\par \par \uc2 "You get better results by pointing a gun to the head," he said.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2018, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2018, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5}}}\par \par \uc2 For TOP NEWS across emerging markets\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-3T09:53:17.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180503ee5300bkw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
