\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's peso weakens sharply despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2018\par 23:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds dollars sold by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, May 2 (Reuters) - Argentina's peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended 3.11 percent weaker on Wednesday at an all-time low of 21.2 per U.S. dollar, even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued selling dollars to try to halt the slide of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sustained weakening showed a lack of investor confidence in Latin America's No. 3 economy, which is blighted by one of the world's highest inflation rates.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold $504.5 million in the spot market on Wednesday, adding to the $3.7 billion it sold in the last three days of last week. The action culminated on Friday in a surprise hike of the bank's key interest rate to 30.25 percent from 27.25. Monday and Tuesday were market holidays.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's local stock index rose 77 percent last year and investors even gobbled up a 100-year bond as President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's strong performance in mid-term elections spurred hopes for more market friendly reforms. But investors have more recently woken up to the country's vulnerabilities.\par \par \uc2 "The forces driving the peso lower are unlikely to abate," \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said in a report on Wednesday, pointing to a current account deficit equivalent to 5 percent of gross domestic product as well as high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Local brokerage Delphos Investment said in a report the recent pace of dollar selling was not sustainable. It also said the implementation of a capital gains tax for foreign investors last month had led to a decrease in foreign capital entering Argentine markets.\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices in Argentina rose 2.3 percent in March, slightly down from the 2.4 percent increase in February. Twelve-month inflation was 25.4 percent, the same level as February. (Reporting by Walter Bianchi, writing by Hugh Bronstein and Caroline Stauffer; editing by Alistair Bell and Sandra Maler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-2T22:36:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180502ee5200mhn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
