\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 ARGENTINA: Merval Falls For The Third Consecutive Session\b0\par\par\uc2 178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Merval, the main index of the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange, fell 0.67% to 30,952.16 points Monday for the third consecutive drop.In spite of an early rise, the Merval changed course after the Argentinean President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  asked municipalities and the provinces to provide a tax break for utility bills.The shares of VALO (-5.30%), Metrogas (-4.51%), Endesa Costanera (-4.42%), Distribuidora de Gas Cuyana (-3.32%), and Transportadora de Gas of the South (-2.48%) closed lower, while Banco Franc?s (1.48%) and Loma (1.21%) rose."There are also doubts about whether the new Capital Markets Legislation should be approved in Congress," said Eduardo Fern?ndez, an analyst at Rava Bursatil.Meanwhile, the locally traded U.S. dollar rose 0.34%, quoted at 20.26 Argentinean pesos, keeping the upward trend and reaching the highest level in recent weeks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA), after a few days away, resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180424ee4n0003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
