\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  surprises market with rate signal\b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 01:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds final prices, details from the region)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, March 22 (Reuters) - Yields on Brazilian interest\par rate futures dropped on Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par unexpectedly indicated it will continue cutting interest rates,\par while fears of a U.S. trade war with China helped put pressure\par on Latin American markets.\par     The bank on Wednesday reduced the benchmark Selic rate by 25\par basis points to an all-time low of 6.50 percent, as widely\par expected.\par     But policymakers were explicit in forecasting another cut at\par their May meeting, contradicting the consensus that this week\par would mark the end of the deepest easing cycle in a decade.\par After that, unless conditions change radically, it would stand\par pat, according to a policy statement.\par     Yields on rate futures fell sharply as traders adjusted\par their bets.\par     "Unless the Brazilian real comes under pressure for domestic\par or external reasons, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be in no hurry to\par begin the tightening cycle," economists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par wrote in a report.\par     The real weakened over 1 percent on concerns that\par lower rates could dampen demand for Brazilian assets. It was the\par biggest loser among Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which suffered\par the effect of growing fears of U.S. protectionism.\par     Brazil's stock exchange, however, fell only 0.25\par percent, as shares of steelmakers jumped after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 United States\par government\f28 \uc2 \f2  suspended a tariff hike on Brazilian steel and\par aluminum imports as it begins bilateral negotiations.\par     Stock markets were down across Latin America after U.S.\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  launched anti-China tariffs, helping to\par push down the Mexican peso by more than 1 percent.\par     Still, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso rose after another \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the market by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     In Peru, the sol rose to its highest level in\par almost two months on news Vice President Martin Vizcarra would\par take power following the resignation on Wednesday of President\par Juan Pablo Kuczynski in the face of near-certain impeachment.\par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2330 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                    Latest       Daily     YTD\par                                                  pct     pct\par                                               change  change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets             1,196.73    -1.07     3.3\par  MSCI LatAm                        3,029.01    -0.62     7.1\par  Brazil Bovespa                   84,767.88    -0.25   10.95\par  Mexico IPC                       47,342.78    -0.34   -4.04\par  Chile IPSA                        5,515.99    -0.35   -0.87\par  Chile IGPA                       27,661.66    -0.32   -1.14\par  Argentina MerVal                 31,908.22    -1.43    6.13\par  Colombia IGBC                    11,439.71    -1.73    0.61\par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  