\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 ARGENTINA: Merval Falls Due To Trade War Fears\b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Merval, the main index of the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange, dropped 1.07% to 32,020.94 points Thursday, in line with the negative mood of global stock markets amid fears of a trade war between the United States and China.President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  unveiled today that the U.S. would adopt new trade barriers to Chinese products. "This measure comes two weeks after Trump imposed duties on steel and aluminum imports, which is why markets today have reacted badly, because the possibility of the launching of a global trade war," said Eduardo Fern?ndez, an analyst at Rava Bursetil.Faced with this scenario, \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  shares were those that stood out, dropping 9.65%, while Aluar gained 1.74%. Meanwhile, the fall in oil prices impacted \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (-3.12%), \uc2 YPF\uc2  (-3.02%) and \uc2 Petrolera Pampa\uc2  (-1.86%).Other shares that closed with heavy losses were \uc2 Transportadora de Gas del Sur\uc2  (-4.28%), Agrometal (-3.71%) and \uc2 Cresud\uc2  (-2.05%).\par \par \uc2  On the positive end, the highest increases were \uc2 Holcim\uc2  (2.88%) and Central Puerto (1.71%).The locally traded U.S. dollar closed down 0.22%, at Argentinean 20.22 pesos, a subtle drop after a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. According to Gustavo Quintana, an analyst at PR Corredores, the "intense official activity caused a further decline in the dollar with sales in the sector where the big players operate."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180322ee3m005cg\