\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-LatAm  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  seesaw on U.S. political woes\b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 03:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds detail on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , closing prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     BRASILIA, March 16 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par seesawed on Friday as speculation that more top Trump\par administration officials could be replaced and concerns U.S.\par trade tariffs could hurt the global economy weighed on demand\par for risky assets.\par     U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  has decided to replace his\par national security adviser, \f28 \uc2 \f2 H.R. McMaster\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Washington Post\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par reported on Thursday. \par     At the same time, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Times\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported U.S. Special\par Counsel Robert Mueller had issued a subpoena for documents\par related to Trump's businesses, including some concerning Russia.\par \par     Earlier this week, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took a hit after Trump\par dismissed Secretary of State \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rex Tillerson\f28 \uc2 \f2  and investors grew\par increasingly nervous about the direction U.S. policy might take\par following a series of departures by key members of staff.\par     "Risk appetite is suffering due to the U.S. political\par scenario, marked by instability in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's cabinet and\par worries about increased protectionism," economists at SulAm\u233\'00\'E9rica\par Investimentos wrote in a report.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Peru, Chile and Colombia\par  slipped between 0.3 and 0.4 percent, while the Argentine\par peso firmed due to an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which sold $413 million in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \par     Meanwhile, Brazil's real firmed by 0.35 percent and\par the Mexican peso closed almost flat. Brazil's benchmark Bovespa\par stock index was down slightly.\par     Shares in wood pulp and paper producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Suzano Papel e\par Celulose SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  surged over 20 percent after it won the\par battle for control of larger rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fibria Celulose SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par , whose shares slumped 10 percent.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 0035 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                               daily %     YTD %\par                                               change    change\par                                    Latest             \par  MSCI Emerging Markets              1213.14    -0.25      4.72\par  MSCI LatAm                         3036.56    -0.38      7.37\par  Brazil Bovespa                    84886.49    -0.05     11.10\par  Mexico IPC                        47477.58    -0.71     -3.80\par  Chile IPSA                         5596.68     0.17      0.58\par  Chile IGPA                        28033.02     0.15      0.19\par  Argentina MerVal                  32555.08    -0.47      8.28\par  Colombia IGBC                     11500.89      0.9      1.15\par                                                               \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                   daily %     YTD %\par                                               change    change\par                                                       \par              