\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The dollar approached yesterday to the 20 pesos after the fall of rates of the Central\b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 So far in January, the dollar in the retail segment rose 1.10 pesos, in a context of increasing demand.\par \par \uc2 The dollar reached a new record yesterday by rising 27 cents in Buenos Aires and closing at 19.43 pesos for the purchase and 19.93 pesos for sale to the public, in a day in which in some banks the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached 20 pesos.\par \par \uc2 In C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba, the price at exchange offices reached 20.30 pesos, but the Bank of Cordoba reported that yesterday's closing was at 19.95 pesos per dollar.\par \par \uc2 So far in January, the dollar in the retail segment rose 1.10 pesos, in a context of increasing demand. The rises were precipitated since Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again cut the Monetary Policy rate by 75 basis points and take it to 27.25 percent, and after that last Monday the president of the entity, \uc2 Federico Sturzenegger\uc2 , gave the signal that real returns are more limited than in recent months.\par \par \uc2 "The banks took the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  72 million dollars to supply the retail market," said Gustavo Quintana, operator of PR Corredores de Cambio, explaining the mechanism that is used to supply the demand.\par \par \uc2 The analyst noted that in practice, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  delivers to the banks an average of 30 million dollars a day - yesterday were more than 70 million - and that these, in return, deposit an equivalent figure abroad and use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  they have in their power to meet the market requirement.\par \par \uc2 In the National Bank, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  advanced 20 cents and traded at 19.30 and 19.80 pesos for the purchase and sale.\par \par \uc2 "The exchange market has accumulated so far in January a 5.37 percent dollar increase, while all of 2017 recorded an increase of 17.36 percent," Izzo added.\par \par \uc2 The economist Christian Buteler indicated that although the exchange rate is floating, at the current level of exchange rate "it is close to the ceiling".\par \par \uc2 "The wholesaler can not exceed 20 pesos, at least in the short term, because it would begin to affect the inflation target. If the rises are violent as was the case, the exchange rate does not only affect those imported components but also the local prices that adjust for the doubts because everything is going up, "Buteler added. In the square, traders expect the dollar to slow its rise or otherwise an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BCRA injecting more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dollar soars, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell yesterday to a new three-year low against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after US Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  said he was pleased with the weakness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the exchange offices in C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba, more than 20\par \par \uc2 The dollar was sold at $ 2.30 in the Cordovan Center.\par \par \uc2 $ 19.95 It was the price set by the \uc2 Banco de C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba\uc2  for the sale. The difference with the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was lower than usual.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180125ee1p000ri\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
