\par\par \b \uc2 Madalena Announces: Spudding of New Well; Appointment of Chairman; Board of Directors\b0\par\par\uc2 1,698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2017\par 13:30\par \uc2 GlobeNewswire\par \uc2 PZON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2017 GlobeNewswire, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Madalena Announces: Spudding of New Well; Appointment of Chairman; Board of Directors\par \par \uc2 CALGARY, Alberta, Oct. 30, 2017 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) --\par \par \uc2 Spudding of new well\par \par \uc2 Madalena Energy Inc\uc2 . ("Madalena" or the "Company") (TSX-V:MVN) (OTCQX:MDLNF) is pleased to announce that their joint-venture partner Pan America Energy LLC ("PAE") successfully started \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spudding of a second horizontal multi-frac well (CAS.x-14) in the Vaca Muerta Shale Formation at the Coiron Amargo Sur Este ("CASE") block in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The CAS.x-14 exploration follows the earlier successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into well CAS.x-15. The program includes drilling horizontally for approximately 1,500 metres in the Vaca Muerta unconventional oil resource play at a vertical depth of approximately 3,100 metres and performing approximately 60 hydraulic fracs with approximately 10,800 klb of proppant.\par \par \uc2 Total gross estimated cost of this re-entry is US$8.3 million, which includes the costs for drilling, completing and equipping the well.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  Update Cas.x-15\par \par \uc2 The results of the last production test on CAS.x-15 yielded 125 boe per day through 3mm choke with 680 psi; Cum Oil Production of 29,200 barrels. Preliminary interpretations of the well results indicate that the well has stabilized at approximately 125 boe per day without artificial lift.\par \par \uc2 Appointment of new Chairman\par \par \uc2 Madalena is also pleased to announce the appointment of \uc2 Mr. Gus Halas\uc2  as Chairman of the Board of Directors. Mr. Halas has been a director of Madalena since January 2015 and has experience serving as a director of Triangle Petroleum Corporation, Optimize RX and School Speciality Inc. Previously, Mr. Halas held positions as Chief Executive Officer and President of Central Garden & Pet Company, and President, Chief Executive Officer and Chairman of the Board of T-3 Energy Services Inc. Madalena Chief Executive Officer \uc2 Mr. Jose Penafiel\uc2  is happy to welcome Mr. Halas in his new role as Chairman: "\uc2 Gus Halas\uc2  provides a wealth of experience in managing businesses in the energy sector. I am pleased to have Mr. Halas as Madalena's Chairman who will provide leadership to help the company achieve its growth objective."\par \par \uc2 Company Board composition\par \par \uc2 The following directors currently serve on the Company's board with Mr. Halas and \uc2 Mr. Jose Penafiel\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Ruben Etcheverry\par \par \uc2 Director - Mr. A. Ruben Etcheverry was the Chief Executive Officer and Chairman of the Board of Gas y Petr\u243\'00\'F3leo de Neuqu\u233\'00\'E9n S.A. (GyP) from its foundation in 2008 to 2013. GyP is the oil & gas provincial company and the holder of all provincial petroleum and gas concessions. He is currently a recognized advisor on energy matters for various private companies and organizations. Mr. Etcheverry has more than 25 years' experience in the energy sector.\par \par \uc2 Ralph Gillcrist\par \par \uc2 Director - Mr. Gillcrist has been the Chief Executive Officer, President and an Executive Director of Oronova Energy Inc. since April 2017. Mr. Gillcrist also served as Executive Director of Petroamerica Oil Corp. ("\uc2 Petroamerica\uc2 ") from January 2015 to January 2016. Mr. Gillcrist previously served as the Chief Executive Officer and President of Petroamerica from January 2015 to January 2016. Prior thereto Mr. Gillcrist served as Chief Operating Officer of Petroamerica since December 2012 and served as its Executive Vice President of Exploration. Mr. Gillcrist has more than 28 years of international oil and gas experience.\par \par \uc2 Barry Larson\par \par \uc2 Director - Chief Executive Officer of Frontera Energy Inc. ("Frontera") since February 2017. Director of Frontera from October 2016 to February 2017. Previously, Vice President, \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Chief Operating Officer of Parex Resources Inc. from September, 2009 to December, 2015. Prior thereto, Vice President \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Chief Operating Officer of Petro Andina Resources Inc. from February, 2005 to September, 2009.\par \par \uc2 Leonardo Madcur\par \par \uc2 Director - Mr. Madcur is currently Director of Corporate Development at the \uc2 Werthein Group\uc2 . Prior to this, from January 2011 until December 2011, he was Chief Financial Officer at Uno Medios/Grupo America. From December 2008 until December 2010, Mr. Madcur was Managing Director at Integra Investment. From January 2007 until November 2008, Mr. Madcur was Investment Manager at \uc2 Corporacion America\uc2 . Previously, he was Secretary of Technical Coordination in \uc2 Argentina's Ministry of Economy\uc2 , Former Regulator of Competition and Consumers, and Former Member of the Board of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Eric Mark\par \par \uc2 Director - Mr. Mark is currently a Managing Director at Batuta Capital Advisors ("Batuta"), a merchant bank targeting middle market and special situation opportunities in both the public and private markets. Prior to joining Batuta, Mr. Mark was a Senior Analyst/Junior Portfolio Manager at BTG Pactual, a Brazilian investment bank, co-managing a $2 billion portfolio of distressed, high yield and special situation equities. Mr. Mark has over 20 years of investment experience (credit and equity) in the energy, metals & mining, general industrials and telecommunications sectors across North America, South America and Europe.\par \par \uc2 Alejandro A. Penafiel\par \par \uc2 Director - Mr. Penafiel worked in U.S. political campaigns prior to entering the energy sector. He has also worked in European energy derivatives markets in sales and business development positions at \uc2 Trayport Ltd\uc2 . then a subsidiary of GFI Inc. He previously headed Hispania Petroleum S.A. ("Hispania") corporate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe and led the day to day \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the group's U.S. investment vehicles focusing on the Permian basin. Mr. Penafiel holds a BA in Economics from The \uc2 American University in Washington\uc2  D.C. and is a CFA Level III candidate.\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 Madalena Energy\par \par \uc2 Madalena is an independent, Canadian upstream oil and gas company with \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in four provinces of Argentina where it is primarily focused on the delineation of unconventional oil and gas resources. The Company is implementing horizontal drilling and completions technology to develop both its conventional and resource plays.\par \par \uc2 Madalena trades on the \uc2 TSX Venture Exchange\uc2  under the symbol MVN and on the OTCQX under the symbol MDLNF.\par \par \uc2 For further information please contact: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Jose David Penafiel                Alejandro Augusto Penafiel \par  Chief Executive Officer            Director \par  email: info@madalenaenergy.com     email: info@madalenaenergy.com \par  phone: (403) 262-1901              phone: (403) 262-1901 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reader Advisories\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Forward Looking Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The information in this news release contains certain forward-looking statements. These statements relate to future events or our future performance, in particular, but not limited to, wi