\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso falls while Latam stocks rise after Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2016\par 22:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MEXICO CITY, Feb 10 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso hit a\par record low on a slump in oil prices on Wednesday while Latin\par American stock markets rose after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief said\par the United States would stick to its plan of "gradual" interest\par rate hikes.\par     The comments from Fed Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  eased concerns\par about the U.S. economy, the world's largest, rallying stock\par markets from Chile to Mexico, for which the United States is the\par biggest export market. \par     Chile's stock market climbed 0.7 percent, while\par Mexico's IPC stock index rallied as much as 1 percent before\par paring gains to close up 0.3 percent to 42,535.74 points.\par     But in Mexico, the region's second-largest economy,\par the peso fell to a historic low of 18.9595 per dollar in a fifth\par straight day of losses, dragged down by volatile crude prices.\par     U.S. crude fell as low as $27.39 a barrel as worries about a\par global supply glut overshadowed data showing a surprise drop in\par U.S. stockpiles. \par     Analysts fret the sharp drop in crude prices since last June\par will dampen prospects of foreign direct investment in Mexico's\par newly opened oil fields. The peso has lost nearly 10 percent so\par far this year, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit\par volatility.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Brazil's stock indexes both\par slipped as investors sold off shares after a two-day market\par holiday.\par \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2100 GMT:\par  Stock indexes               Latest          Daily   YTD pct\par                                                pct    change\par                                             change  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            732.36      0.34     -8.09\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                     1,712.97     -0.36     -6.04\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                40,376.58     -0.53     -6.86\par  Mexico IPC                    42,535.74      0.32     -1.03\par  Chile IPSA                     3,675.67      0.73     -0.12\par  Chile IGPA                    18,060.50      0.65     -0.50\par  Argentina MerVal              11,346.76     -0.46     -2.81\par  Colombia IGBC                  8,731.30      0.22      2.15\par  Venezuela IBC                 14,583.27      1.47     -0.03\par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                        Latest     Daily   YTD pct\par                                                pct    change\par                                             change  \par  Brazil real                      3.9348     -0.82      0.31\par  Mexico peso                     18.8890     -0.47     -9.63\par  Chile peso                        712.9     -0.10     -0.45\par  Colombia peso                  3,390.59      0.03     -6.98\par  Peru sol                         3.5061     -0.11     -2.70\par  Argentina peso (interbank)      14.4900     -0.84    -11.61\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (parallel)          14.2      0.42      0.49\par                                                     \par  \par  (Reporting by Anna Yukhananov; Editing by Leslie Adler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 20