\par\par \b \uc2 *S&P Takes Several Rating Actions On 12 Argentine Companies\b0\par\par\uc2 2,491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2016\par 00:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 3 Feb 2016 18:25 ET  Press Release: S&P Takes Several Rating Actions On 12 Argentine Companies\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \par  \par      -- On Feb. 3, 2016, we raised our local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on Argentina to \par 'B-' from 'CCC+'. The outlook on this rating is stable. At the same time, we \par revised upward our transfer and convertibility (T&C) on the country to 'B-' \par from 'CCC-'. \par      -- We're taking various positive rating actions on 12 Argentine \par companies. \par      -- The outlook on these companies is now stable, mirroring that on the \par sovereign's local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating and our view of a new policy approach that \par addresses Argentina's main economic imbalances. \par  \par BUENOS AIRES (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) Feb. 3, 2016--Standard & Poor's Ratings \par Services raised its local and foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on the following \par companies and utilities to 'B-'. The outlook on these ratings is stable: \par  \par      -- Aeropuertos Argentina 2000 S.A. (AA2000); \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 IRSA Propiedades Comerciales S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (IRCP); \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 IRSA Inversiones y Representaciones S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (IRSA); \par      -- CLISA-Compania Latinoamericana de Infraestructura & Servicios S.A.; \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mastellone Hermanos S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 .; \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 CAPEX S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 .; and \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Transportadora de Gas del Sur S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 .(TGS). \par  \par We placed our 'B-' local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on Arauco Argentina S.A on \par CreditWatch with positive implications. In addition, we raised our foreign \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on the company to 'B-' from 'CCC-'. The outlook on this rating \par is stable. \par  \par We raised our foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras Argentina S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (PESA) to \par 'B-' from 'CCC-'. The outlook is stable. \par  \par We also raised our local and foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on the following \par utilities to 'CCC' from 'CCC-': \par  \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Metrogas S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 .; \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Compania de Transporte de Energia Electrica en Alta Tension Transener \par S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (Transener); and \par      -- Empresa Distribuidora Y Comercializadora Norte S.A. (EDENOR). \par  \par The outlook on Metrogas and EDENOR is stable, while the outlook on Transener \par is positive. \par  \par The rating actions follow the raising of the sovereign's local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating \par to 'B-' from 'CCC+' and the revision of our T&C assessment on Argentina to \par 'B-' from 'CCC-'. The sovereign foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on Argentina remain \par at 'SD/SD'. \par  \par The rating action on the sovereign reflects recent steps to address some of \par the substantial economic imbalances prevailing in Argentina. The recently \par elected President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mauricio Macri\f28 \uc2 \f2  aims to reduce these imbalances over the next \par four years, reaching a balanced budget by 2019. The revision of the T&C \par assessment reflects the rapid and successful liberalization of the exchange \par rate market in the country. While this is only the beginning of a long \par process, we believe the sovereign is now unlikely to interfere with access to \par and transfer of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .. The new leadership at Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also set an ambitious goal of implementing an inflation targeting \par regime throughout the term of the administration. The outlook revision on the \par sovereign's local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating balances the improvement of economic \par policies with the political challenges facing the new Administration. We \par expect the government to implement policies that gradually contain \par inflationary pressures and reduce its fiscal deficit, slowly strengthening the \par macroeconomic pillars of the economy.  (please see "Argentina Local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par Ratings Raised To 'B-/B'; Outlook Stable; Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Ratings Remain \par 'SD/SD'," published on Feb 3, 2016). \par  \par We raised the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on the seven Argentine companies, \par reflecting lower risks of the government actions exacerbating operating \par conditions for these entities. Their individual credit profiles wouldn't allow \par them to have a higher rating than the sovereign's local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating. \par  \par We raised the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on these entities because the lower \par risk of the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange market \par has reduced the risk of these entities not meeting their foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par denominated obligations according to original terms and conditions. This in \par turn lowers the risk of local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  creditors accelerating their lending \par due to the entities' inability to meet their commitments. We continue to \par believe that the T&C assessment is the key risk for entities operating in the \par country because none of them would be able to continue honoring their foreign \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  obligations under potential restrictions to access to foreign \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and/or restrictions on the ability to transfer money abroad. \par  \par The upgrade of PESA reflects the lower T&C risk. \par  \par The rating action on Arauco \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reflects the lower risk of the \par government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the company's ability to meet foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par denominated obligations under original terms and conditions. The local \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on this company is now at the same level of the sovereign's \par long-term local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating, reflecting our view of the former's ability \par to generate local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to meet all its financial obligations, regardless \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denomination. The CreditWatch positive listing on this rating \par reflects at least a 50% chance for an upgrade in the next 90 days. In \par resolving this CreditWatch, we will be incorporating additional information \par related to potential macroeconomic risks associated with a further stressed \par scenario for the sovereign to determine if Arauco Argentina can have a higher \par rating than the sovereign's local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating. We see the upgrade \par potential limited to one notch. \par  \par The upgrade of Transener, EDENOR, and Metrogas reflects our view of a less \par imminent path to default due to the recently announced measures in the \par country's energy sector. Nevertheless, the ratings continue to reflect the \par current delicate and weak credit standing of these entities, which would \par likely default if structural market conditions don't change. \par  \par Despite the positive rating actions, our credit perception of risks remains \par high for these entities. Furthermore, we believe sustainable growth for the \par domestic corporate sector depends on greater regulatory certainty and \par improving business climate for long-term investment. The upgrade potential for \par Argentine companies remains limited due to the institutional environment in \par the country and the exposure of certain companies and sectors to specific \par factors such as regulatory uncertainty, discretional political interference, \par high inflation, and debt-revenue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mismatch. All of these factors \par affect, in varying degrees, both the local and foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on \par Argentine companies. In addition, the ratings on regulated companies are \par heavily influenced by our view of regulatory risk. Most of the concession \par contracts of rated utilities are still pending a full renegotiation, which is \par a major credit concern, in our view. \par  \par The stable outlook on AA2000, IRCP, IRSA, CLISA, Mastellone, CAPEX, EDENOR, \par PESA, Metrogas and TGS now mirrors that on the sovereign's local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par rating. It also reflects the new policy approach that addresses Argentina's \par main economic imbalances. It also recognizes the political challenges the new \par administration will still have to face. Addressing economic dislocations-amid \par Brazil's recession and its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's steep depreciation, lower agricultural \par commodity prices, and uncertainty about China's growth prospects and the U.S. \par monetary tightening--will slow Argentina's economic recovery. \par  \par The positive outlook on Transener reflects our expectation of one-in-three \par chances of an upgrade following the likely improvement in business conditions \par due to the Ministry of Energy's recent announcements of changes in the sector \par and a gradual strengthening of the regulatory framework, which should help \par bolster the company's credit metrics and liquidity. \par  \par We could further upgrade AA2000, IRSA, IRCP, CLISA, Mastellone, CAPEX, EDENOR, \par Metrogas, and TGS if the T&C is further positively reviewed. In addition, an \par improvement in the economic environment for the corporate sector in the \par country could lead to more predictable and favorable business conditions for \par Argentine companies, which would also translate to stronger business risk \par profile assessments that in turn could also benefit the credit quality of the \par entities. \par  \par We could upgrade EDENOR, Transener, and Metrogas if we perceive that the \par changes in regulations are effective in promoting more sustainable capital \par structures, which would reduce exposure to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuations--due \par to their dollar-denominated debt--and boost cash flow generation. \par  \par A downward change in our T&C assessment would most likely result in a \par downgrade of all 12 companies because we believe that the corporate sector's \par ability to honor its foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  obligations is related to this \par assessment. In such scenario, we would analyze the companies' ability to cope \par with the sovereign preventing them from accessing and transferring foreign \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  abroad. \par  \par RELATED CRITERIA AND RESEARCH \par  \par Related Criteria \par      -- Methodology And Assumptions: Liquidity Descriptors For Global \par Corporate Issuers, Dec. 16, 2014 \par      -- Corporate Methodology, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Corporate Methodology: Ratios and Adjustments, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Group Rating Methodology, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Country Risk Assessment Methodology And Assumptions, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Methodology: Industry Risk, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Ratings Above the Sovereign - Corporate and Government Ratings: \par Methodology and Assumptions, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- General Criteria: Methodology: Management And Governance Credit \par Factors For Corporate Entities And Insurers, Nov. 13, 2012 \par      -- Criteria For Assigning 'CCC+', 'CCC', 'CCC-', And 'CC' Ratings, Oct. \par 1, 2012 \par      -- Use Of CreditWatch And Outlooks, Sept. 14, 2009 \par      -- 2008 Corporate Criteria: Rating Each Issue, April, 15, 2008 \par  \par Certain terms used in this report, particularly certain adjectives used to \par express our view on rating relevant factors, have specific meanings ascribed \par to them in our criteria, and should therefore be read in conjunction with such \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3 Feb 2016 18:26 ET \par Press Release: S&P Takes Several Rating Actions -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par criteria. Please see Ratings Criteria at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.standardandpoors.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.standardandpoors.com}}}\uc2 \f2  for further \pa