\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Peso Sinks After  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Controls Lifted\b0\par\par\uc2 By Taos Turner   \par \uc2 1,091 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Dezember 2015\par 09:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES--Argentina's peso lost more than a quarter of its value against the U.S. dollar Thursday, a day after the new government of President Mauricio Macri said it would lift \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls to attract investors and kick-start the economy.\par \par \uc2 Within minutes of trading, the peso weakened to 13.9 per dollar from 9.8 the previous day, its biggest percentage decline since January 2002, following the abandonment of the peso-dollar parity. The move lower will hit multinationals that operate in Argentina and ordinary Argentines who will see the value of their savings cut in dollar terms.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday in New York, the dollar bought 13.3085 pesos, from 9.8164 pesos late Wednesday, down 26% on the day and 36% for the year.\par \par \uc2 Economists had expected Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken following Wednesday's news that the government was ending a four-year policy of strict limits on the sale of U.S. dollars, a policy that restricted imports, hurt economic growth and spawned a thriving black market in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The previous black-market rate on Wednesday was about 14.50 pesos to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 In the days since he took office, Mr. Macri has moved quickly to undo the economic legacy of 12 years of populist policies by his predecessors, \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2  and her late husband, N\u233\'00\'E9stor. The pair expanded the government's role in the economy, including nationalizing some companies, expanding subsidies and launching price controls.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Macri's administration has eliminated most farm export taxes, cut personal income taxes, begun restaffing Argentina's discredited statistics agency, and replaced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president.\par \par \uc2 But scrapping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls is the biggest move so far and one that will shape the coming months of his administration.\par \par \uc2 The decision to let the peso float is aimed at sparking growth by getting Argentina's agribusiness sector to start exporting again due to a more competitive exchange rate. Those exports will bring badly needed dollars to the country. It also is aimed at giving a jolt of confidence to investors.\par \par \uc2 The key in coming days will be whether the \uc2 Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from sliding further and entering an unpredictable tumble. To keep the lid on price increases and attract investment, Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday raised its benchmark rate as high as 38%.\par \par \uc2 "We are still going through the process of price discovery," said Goldman Sachs economist Alberto Ramos. "The fact that there wasn't a crazy move early in the morning to 15.50 or 16, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to show its hand very quickly, is in itself evidence that they prepared the ground relatively well and communicated the move relatively well to make this a successful experiment."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 According to one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, volume was low in U.S. dollar-peso trading due to problems that banks and other market makers had in reprogramming their operating software to accommodate new \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations. The trader said volume and demand will increase after these adjustments, adding he believes the peso will then fall further.\par \par \uc2 Other economists said they expected the move to succeed in the short term.\par \par \uc2 "I don't expect to see strong pressures on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the short term, as an adjustment in the exchange rate to 14 or 15 pesos per dollar has been already assimilated," said Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Machinea, who served as Argentina's economy minister from 1999 to 2001.\par \par \uc2 "A lot will depend on inflationary pressures over the next two months, as the government has implemented several policy measures at once that could have a strong impact on prices, just as unions prepare for wage negotiations early next year," he said.\par \par \uc2 Many ordinary Argentines, accustomed to their country's long history of financial booms and busts, said they anticipated the decline, which is expected to raise the country's 25% inflation rate by making imports more expensive in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  terms.\par \par \uc2 "Even at 14 pesos the exchange rate is still cheap; that's what it costs to buy a bar of chocolate," said Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Mata, an immigrant from Venezuela who works at a record store. "Like it or not, prices are going to go up here. But I've seen how \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls ruined my home country and getting rid of them will help Argentina's economy. "\par \par \uc2 Retailers and their suppliers have been marking up prices in anticipation of a devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Retail prices rose 1.2% in the first week of December alone, the fastest clip since Argentina devalued the peso by 20% in January 2014, according to Elypsis, an economic research firm.\par \par \uc2 Still, the move to let the peso float freely is fraught with risks. For many in Latin America, the price of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollars is seen as a gauge of economic well-being.\par \par \uc2 "The losers from this are Argentine consumers that will now face a higher import bill, foreign investors that have assets in Argentine pesos--they're the textbook losers--and Argentine companies that have dollar debts but revenue streams in Argentine pesos," said Neil Shearing, chief emerging-markets economist at Capital Economics.\par \par \uc2 Argentina doesn't have deep dollar reserves to defend the peso, by buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up its price against the greenback. Over the past four years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have plummeted to about $24 billion from more than $52 billion. Economists said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real net reserves are far lower considering liabilities such as money owed to importers and outstanding bond payments.\par \par \uc2 To ease those fears, Finance Minister Alfonso Prat-Gay said Wednesday that Argentina is on track to obtain between $15 billion and $25 billion in cash from agreements with international banks, grain exporters and \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still, one of the underlying problems for the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in addition to inflation, is Argentina's gap between what it spends and takes in, a shortfall surpassing 7% of annual economic output. That difference has until now been made up by stimulus measures, fueling inflation. Mr. Macri has promised to trim the deficit and has already announced cuts to fuel subsidies.\par \par \uc2 Alberto Messer in Buenos Aires, Ryan Dube in Lima, Peru, and Julie Wernau in New York contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Taos Turner at taos.turner@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 25-12-15 0834GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020151225ebcp0002o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
