ptions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On January 31, 2014, Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n entered into a syndicated loan agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Industrial and Commercial Bank of China (Argentina) \f28 \uc2 \f2 S.A. ("ICBC") and Banco Ita\u250\'00\'FA Argentina S.A. for Ps. 100 million, at a variable rate of adjusted BADLAR + 5.25%, with final maturity in July 2015, for the purpose of paying a portion of the USD 59 million principal amount due on Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n's notes which were paid by Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n in February 2014. As of December 31, 2014, Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n cancelled Ps. 40 million principal amount under the syndicated loan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On March 12, 2014, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco de la Ciudad de Buenos Aires\f28 \uc2 \f2  ("Banco Ciudad") joined the syndicated loan agreement executed by Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n on January 31, 2014 with ICBC and Banco Ita\u250\'00\'FA Argentina S.A. as lender, thereby agreeing to make a disbursement of Ps. 50 million in favor of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n at a variable rate of adjusted BADLAR + 5.25% with final maturity in the month of July 2015. To that end, Banco Ciudad executed an amendment to that agreement whereby it irrevocably accepted and agreed to each and every one of its terms and conditions. As of December 31, 2014, that company cancelled Ps. 20 million principal amount under the syndicated loan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On April 21, 2014, within the framework of the syndicated loan agreement executed on January 31, 2014, the banks ICBC and Banco Ita\u250\'00\'FA Argentina S.A. made new disbursements for an aggregate amount of Ps. 100 million at a variable rate of adjusted BADLAR + 5.25%. Final maturity is in July 2015. As of December 31, 2014, Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n cancelled Ps. 40 million principal amount under the syndicated loan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result of the execution of the syndicated loan agreement, Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n has undertaken certain covenants, including: (i) limitation on the issuance of guarantees by subsidiaries and encumbrances; (ii) reorganization, change of control, and sale of assets under certain conditions, (iii) limitation on incurring debt above certain approved ratios, (iv) limitation on capital investment exceeding certain amount, and (v) limitation on transactions with shareholders and affiliates under certain conditions. [ 18-03-15 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On January 30, 2015, the Company entered into a syndicated loan agreement with ICBC, Ita\u250\'00\'FA, Banco Ciudad, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Santander R\u237\'00\'EDo S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . ("Santander") and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Macro S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . ("Macro") for Ps. 700 million, at a variable rate of adjusted BADLAR + 4.85%, with final maturity in July 2016, for the purpose of making a prepayment of principal and interest owed to ICBC, Ita\u250\'00\'FA and Banco Ciudad under the syndicated loan agreement executed on January 31, 2014, and in order to finance working capital and capital investments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On April 28, 2014, at the Annual General Ordinary and Extraordinary Shareholders' Meeting of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n, the shareholders of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n approved, among other matters: i) The creation of a Global Program for the issuance of simple, non-convertible, medium or long-term notes, to be authorized by the CNV, to be issued in one or more classes and/or series for an aggregate principal amount including all classes and/or series outstanding under the Program of up to USD 500,000,000, pursuant to the provisions of the Notes Law No. 23,576, as amended. The shareholders delegated on the Board of Directors of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n the power to determine and establish all the other terms for each class and/or series of notes to be issued under this Program. The shareholders also delegated on the Board of Directors of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n the power to approve the terms of the agreements related to the issuance and placement of the notes to be issued under the Program. The Board of Directors of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n may subdelegate all or some powers interchangeably to one or more directors or managers of such company; and ii) the creation of a global program for the issuance of Short-Term Debt Securities of up to USD 100,000,000 (or its equivalent in other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as determined by the Board of Directors) (Valores Representativos de Deuda de Corto Plazo, "VCPs", for its Spanish acronym), and the related registration of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n before the special registry created by the CNV for such purpose. The VCPs will have maturities of up to one year and are to be issued in one or more classes and/or series, under the form of promissory notes subject to the Notes Law No. 23,576, as amended. The shareholders delegated on that company's Board of Directors the power to determine and establish all the other terms of the VCP Program and the classes and/or series of VCPs to be issued within the authorized amount. They also delegated on the Board of Directors the power to request the CNV to register Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n in the Special Registry for VCP Programs and to authorize the VCP Program. The Board of Directors of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n may subdelegate all or some powers interchangeably to one or more directors or managers of such company. As of the date of these financial statements, the Company has not made any filings with the CNV to make such placement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On August 26, 2014, Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n executed a financial loan agreement with Nuevo Banco de Santa Fe S.A. for Ps. 50 million at an annual fixed nominal interest rate of 28% with final maturity in January 2015, for the purpose of increasing its working capital to finance the development of its main corporate business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On January 5, 2015, the Board of Directors of Cablevisi\u243\'00\'F3n decided to call an Ordinary 