\par\par \b \uc2 P&G\uc2  will not lay off staff in Argentina due to tax probe -source\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sarah Marsh  \par \uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2014\par 23:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Nov 4 (Reuters) - \uc2 Procter & Gamble Co\uc2 , the world's No. 1 household products maker, has no plans to lay off staff in Argentina despite having to suspend commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country while it grapples with a tax fraud probe, a source familiar with the matter said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 P&G\uc2  employees are showing up for work and carrying out tasks not related to the sale and purchase of goods, while the company continues talks with the Argentine tax authority, AFIP, in an attempt to defuse the situation, the source told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Argentina accused \uc2 P&G\uc2  on Sunday of hiding income and over-billing $138 million in imports to get money out of the South American country, which has stringent capital controls in place to protect its fast-dwindling foreign reserves.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leftist government, which favors strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the private sector, has publicly accused a host of major foreign companies such as global grains exporters Bunge and Cargill of evading taxes over the past few years.\par \par \uc2 Such investigations are usually resolved with a hefty fine, with the companies resuming business as usual before any real toll is taken on \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  or profits.\par \par \uc2 "It is commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have been stopped. The company cannot import, export or sell its products. But that does not affect day-to-day work at \uc2 P&G\uc2 ," the source said. "Employees continue to work and there are no thoughts of firing anyone."\par \par \uc2 Many other companies including foreign giants such as Anglo-Dutch \uc2 Unilever\uc2  supply Argentine supermarkets with some of the same household goods as \uc2 P&G\uc2 , meaning that even if the tax probe drags on, there is little risk of shortages.\par \par \uc2 P&G\uc2 , which earlier this year came under the scrutiny of Mexican authorities for alleged tax avoidance, said on Monday it had paid all taxes owed in Argentina but was "working to more fully understand the concerns and to constructively resolve them".\par \par \uc2 Cincinnati, Ohio-based \uc2 P&G\uc2 , maker of Gillette razors and Tide detergent, has more than 1,200 employees in Argentina, where it runs three manufacturing plants and two distribution centers.\par \par \uc2 The company's Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  contribute about 1 percent to its overall sales. \uc2 P&G\uc2  reported net sales of $83.1 billion in 2014.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cash-strapped government has been ramping up state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy, Latin America's third largest, in an attempt to prevent its latest debt default from triggering a balance of payments crisis.\par \par \uc2 The country has been banished from international capital markets since its 2002 default on about $100 billion in bonds, compounded by a fresh default on restructured bonds in July.\par \par \uc2 The government is restraining access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to retain \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which have fallen 17 percent over the last 12 months to about $28 billion. (Additional reporting by Hugh Bronstein and Eliana Razsewski; Editing by Peter Galloway) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-4T23:30:49.000Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141104eab400m2z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
