\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 P&G\uc2  halts  \highlight22\uc2 operations \highlight\uc2 , starts talks with Argentina over tax fraud charge\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2014\par 02:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details on \uc2 P&G\uc2  halting \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina, details on impact)\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Nov 3 (Reuters) - \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2  said on Monday it had temporarily suspended \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina after the country's tax authority, which has accused the company of tax fraud, said it started meetings with the world's No.1 household products maker.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Argentina accused the company of hiding income and over-billing $138 million in imports to get money out of the country, which three years ago introduced stringent capital controls in order to protect its fast-dwindling foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 "I can confirm that we have temporarily suspended \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina," spokesman \uc2 Paul Fox\uc2  told Reuters, without giving any other details.\par \par \uc2 Cincinnati-based \uc2 P&G\uc2 , the maker of Gillette razors and Tide detergent, runs three manufacturing plants and two distribution centers in Argentina.\par \par \uc2 P&G\uc2 , which earlier this year came under the scrutiny of Mexican authorities for alleged tax avoidance, said on Monday it had paid all the taxes owed but was "working to more fully understand the concerns and to constructively resolve them."\par \par \uc2 "If \uc2 P&G\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina were suspended for a long period of time, it would make the upper end of 4-6 percent core EPS guidance more difficult to reach," \uc2 BMO\uc2  Capital Markets said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Argentine AFIP tax authority said at the weekend it had suspended \uc2 P&G\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina, retracting its right to export and import.\par \par \uc2 The company said on Monday its Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  contributed about 1 percent to its overall sales. \uc2 P&G\uc2  reported net sales of $83.1 billion in 2014.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's leftist government has been stepping up state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy in an attempt to prevent its latest debt default from triggering a balance of payments crisis.\par \par \uc2 The country has been banished from international capital markets since its 2002 default on about $100 billion in bonds, compounded by its fresh default on restructured bonds in July.\par \par \uc2 The government is restraining access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to retain \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which have fallen 17 percent over the last 12 months, to about $28 billion. (Reporting by Sarah Marsh and Jorge Otaola in Buenos Aires and Nandita Bose in Chicago; Editing by Lisa Shumaker and Ken Wills) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-4T02:19:09.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141104eab40013c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
