\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Fitch: Argentine Banks Will Absorb New Caps on Lending Rate\b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2014\par 14:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeat for additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 June 13 (Reuters) - (The following statement was released by the rating agency)\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to ease borrowing conditions by setting caps on the interest rates and fees charged by banks on consumer loans should not be a major challenge to the affected banks' ratings, according to \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2 . The impacted banks maintain good asset quality and capitalization levels with adequate profitability, even after adjusting for the country's very high inflation. Ratings on Argentina's banks are constrained to no higher than 'B-' by Argentina's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign rating (B-, Negative Outlook).\par \par \uc2 Though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action is clearly not friendly to the nation's banking sector, Fitch does not believe it represents a material challenge to local banks. The move essentially limits their room to further maneuver, should additional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures be implemented.\par \par \uc2 Since 2012, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sovereign rating was downgraded, Fitch has factored potential government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  into bank rating assessments. That rating change was driven by increased state tightening of capital controls and the inability of certain provinces to access U.S. dollars to repay their dollar-denominated debt under local law.\par \par \uc2 We are also not surprised by the action, as other Latin American central banks in Venezuela, Ecuador and Bolivia have taken such monetary steps in the past.\par \par \uc2 Over time, we believe Argentina's banks will adjust to this limitation and find ways to compensate for the income it will forgo. Nonetheless, the risk remains for further government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could materially challenge the banks. \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-13T13:12:53.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140613ea6d00er1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw202\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3030\pichgoal600
