\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2014\par 02:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SALES OF NEW HOMES HIT A COLD SPELL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New-home sales ended 2013 on a weak note amid unusually cold weather, renewing concerns about the housing industry's rebound. (published 0037 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OBAMA TRIES NEW TACK FOR LONG-TERM JOBLESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama is trying to accomplish through voluntary pledges what many lawmakers have tried to do for years with little success: banning companies from refusing to hire people just because they have been out of work for a while. (published 0032 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOVERNMENT REACHES DATA DEAL WITH TECH FIRMS -- UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration has struck a tentative deal with major Internet companies allowing them to tell the public more details about how the government collects data on their customers, officials said Monday. (published 2241 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BIPARTISAN AGREEMENT REACHED ON FARM BILL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Congress moved closer to ending the two-year struggle to pass a new farm bill when senior lawmakers Monday unveiled a bipartisan agreement overhauling agriculture policy for the next five years. (published 0030 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA BUSINESS CONDITIONS IMPROVE, CONFIDENCE STILL STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business conditions improved sharply last month, driving a performance gauge to the highest level in two-and-a-half years. (published 0031 GMT) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ARGENTINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  EASES RULES, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN BID TO DEFEND PESO \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government on Monday tried to prevent last week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation from turning into a financial crisis by allowing Argentines to swap some of their pesos for dollars online, but there were signs the move could fall short. (published 0032 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TURKISH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO MEET ON LIRA CONCERNS -- UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Turkish lira rebounded strongly after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would schedule an extraordinary policy meeting on Tuesday to evaluate recent developments and take necessary measures to ensure price stability. (published 2308 GMT Monday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 27, 2014 20:00 ET (01:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140128ea1s0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
