\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Stocks Gain Slightly as \uc2 Banco Macro Leads\b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2012\par 01:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Banco Macro\uc2  leads Argentina's stocks higher following a positive earnings report\par \par \uc2 --Black-market peso is stable versus the dollar, while the official rate barely moves\par \par \uc2 --Bonds end mixed\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Taos Turner \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUENOS AIRES--Argentine stocks got a boost Wednesday from a positive earnings report from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Macro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BMA.BA, BMA), which helped lift the Merval index.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Merval rose 0.29% to 2458.81 in volume totaling ARS45.5 million Argentine pesos ($9.9 million).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banco Macro\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which posted its second-quarter results the previous evening, rose 3.8% to ARS8.65 Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank reported a net profit of 332 million pesos, up 29% from a year ago. Its lending to the private sector rose 3% on the quarter to ARS26.2 billion, and total deposits rose 3% to ARS33.6 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other movers included financial group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL), which rose 0.6% to ARS3.25, and steel producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tenaris SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (TS, TEN.MI), which fell 0.4% to ARS133.60. Shares of state-run oil and gas company \f28 \uc2 \f2 YPF SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (YPFD.BA, \f28 \uc2 \f2 YPF\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) led the declines with a 2.7% drop to ARS76.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bonds were mixed. The price of the Boden 2015 fell 1.2% to ARS576, while the AA17 bond price fell 0.97% to ARS512.01. The TVPP GDP warrant rose 1.34% to ARS12.83.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The official exchange rate closed at ARS4.5975 to the dollar on the MAE local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wholesale market, compared with ARS4.5955 in the previous session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regularly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, buying dollars to build its international reserves and to keep the peso on a slow path of depreciation against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since early May, authorities have limited dollar sales severely to beef up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's hard-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, fueling a black market for dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar traded for about ARS6.25 in the black market, little changed from the previous session, according to newspaper El Cronista.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Taos Turner at taos.turner@dowjones.com [ 08-08-12 2320GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020120808e8880000y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
