\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Bonds, Stocks Track Offshore Markets Higher\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2012\par 23:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES--Argentina's bonds and stocks tracked gains in offshore markets Monday, as a brief pause in the European debt crisis and last week's strong U.S. economic data lifted emerging-market assets.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are looking pretty good this week. Europe is catching up and putting the ECB statement behind it. U.S. data also came out pretty good last Thursday and Friday," said Brian Joseph, a senior trader at Puente brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local fixed-income market was 446.8 million pesos ($97 million million), accounting for almost 74% of the total volume of securities traded on the exchange.\par \par \uc2 The Bonar X closed 0.3% higher in price terms at ARS520.00, yielding 4.4%.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2015 rose 0.1% to ARS581.50, yielding 13.1%.\par \par \uc2 The 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrant fell 0.3% to ARS12.60.\par \par \uc2 Last Friday, Argentina's government made the final payment of $2.2 billion on its Boden 2012 bond.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Joseph thinks that at least 50% of the Boden payment will get ploughed back into the market by investors looking to take advantage of high-yielding provincial and sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 "I see more value in provincial debt that is trading wider to the sovereign than before the [Sept.-Oct. European] crisis," he said. "There is still more catch-up to do in the provincial side than the sovereign side."\par \par \uc2 The peso weakened to close at ARS4.5925 to the U.S. dollar on the MAE \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  wholesale market, compared with ARS4.5880 Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollars to build its international reserves and to keep the peso on a slow path of depreciation against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Local brokerage Puente said in a note to clients the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $40 million dollars during a session, in which $320 million changed hands.\par \par \uc2 Since early May, authorities have severely limited dollar sales to businesses and individuals to beef up the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which has fueled a vibrant black market for dollars.\par \par \uc2 According to the newspaper El Cronista, the dollar fetched between ARS6.20 and ARS6.24 on the black market Monday.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's benchmark Merval stock index closed 1.1% higher at 2422.92 on volume of ARS31.2 million.\par \par \uc2 Steel-tube maker \uc2 Tenaris SA\uc2  (TS, TS.BA) closed 1.3% higher at ARS133.60; state-controlled oil-and-gas company \uc2 YPF SA\uc2  (\uc2 YPF\uc2 , YPFD.BA) rose 2.9% to ARS78.00; banking group \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL, GGAL.BA) rose 0.6% to ARS3.13; and phone company \uc2 Telecom Argentina SA\uc2  (TEO, TECO2.BA) closed 1% higher at ARS15.35.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ken Parks at ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 06-08-12 2153GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120806e88600164\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
