\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Stocks Up, Bonds Lower as Stimulus Chatter Fails To Convince\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2012\par 23:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks posted slight gains, while benchmark bonds closed lower on Thursday, as a rate cut in China and talk of global \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stimulus failed to ignite a rally in local assets.\par \par \uc2 The Merval index closed 0.3% higher at 2227.58 on light volume of 35.6 million pesos ($7.9 million).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2  (ARGT), which tracks shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, rose 1.9% to $8.12 in New York.\par \par \uc2 Major stock markets in Europe closed broadly higher after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a surprise rate cut, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average gave up most of its early gains to close 0.4% higher.\par \par \uc2 "There was a lot of talk about more stimulus [in major economies]. But investors obviously didn't bite in the absence of concrete actions on that front," said Lautaro Marra, a trader at Bull Market Brokers.\par \par \uc2 Marra said the dollar-denominated Boden 2015 bond offers good yields for investors who want exposure to the greenback, while shares of steel tube maker \uc2 Tenaris SA\uc2  (TS, TS.BA) and Brazilian oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  SA (PBR, PETR4.BR, APBR.BA) are attractive because most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are outside Argentina.\par \par \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  rose 4.3% to ARS102.00; \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  closed 4.0% higher at ARS62.40; and Argentina's largest oil and gas producer, \uc2 YPF SA\uc2  (\uc2 YPF\uc2 , YPFD.BA), rose 0.5% to ARS76.45.\par \par \uc2 Among declining issues, banking concern \uc2 Banco Macro SA\uc2  (BMA, BMA.BA) fell 3.4% to ARS7.95, while cross-town rival \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL, GGAL.BA) lost 2.1% to close at ARS2.82.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local fixed-income market was ARS549.7 million, accounting for about 72% of the total volume of securities traded on the exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 The Bonar X closed 0.1% lower in price terms at ARS425.00, yielding 8.84%.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2015 fell 0.9% to ARS473.50, yielding 5.71%.\par \par \uc2 The 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrant fell 1.6% to close at ARS10.95, and dollar GDP warrants closed 1.7% lower at ARS58.51.\par \par \uc2 The peso firmed to close at ARS4.4863 to the U.S. dollar, compared to ARS4.4903/dollar at Wednesday's close, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollars to build its international reserves and keeping the peso on a slow path of depreciation against the greenback to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Ken Parks at ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 07-06-12 2107GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120607e8670013s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw202\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3030\pichgoal600
