\par\par \b \uc2 Brazilian Real, Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Fall; Debt Little Changed\b0\par\par\uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2012\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaken broadly\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real erases 2012 gains on ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Emerging-market debt is little changed but \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  underperforms\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Erin McCarthy \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real led emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' fall Wednesday, while debt held steady, as concerns about the euro-zone debt crisis dominated markets and investors focused on ongoing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Brazil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets were anxiously gearing up for a Spanish bond auction Thursday, after Spain's borrowing costs rose in an auction earlier this week. Rising Spanish government bond yields have made the country the latest focal point of the euro-zone debt saga, especially as it struggles to rein in its fiscal deficit through tough austerity measures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I do get a sense that there's a little bit of nervousness as there's a Spanish auction tomorrow," said Win Thin, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2 's global head of emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Broader market concerns modestly weighed down emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Mexican peso and South African rand, which often takes cues from market sentiment. Emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate decisions were also in focus, with a string of policy-setting meetings this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real, however, stood out, as it erased all of its 2012 gains Wednesday on ongoing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The dollar climbed to BRL1.8827, marking the real's weakest level since Dec. 29, 2011. Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market twice Wednesday to buy dollars. Brazil's Treasury also issued a sovereign bond denominated in reais in the international market this week, in part to help in the fight against the real appreciation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This "more aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " and is "not good for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Thin said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors also were waiting for Brazil's rate decision Wednesday night. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to cut the Selic benchmark rate by 75 basis points to nine basis points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere in the region, the Mexican peso slipped in line with U.S. stocks. It fell 0.4%, with the dollar buying MXN13.1616 late Wednesday, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South African rand slipped 0.3% against the dollar, which traded at ZAR7.8356. Earlier Wednesday, data showed inflation in South Africa slowed to 6.0% on the year in March from 6.1% in February.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Turkish lira, meanwhile, held up relatively well compared with other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' broad decline. The dollar traded flat on the day against the lira, at TRY1.7890. A more hawkish tone from Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  provided support for the lira, analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday held all its key policy rates steady, in line with expectations, but warned it may have to tighten market interest rates more regularly to curb rising inflation spurred by higher oil prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging-market sovereign debt, meanwhile, was little changed on the day, in line with listless trading in U.S. Treasurys. The risk premium on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, widened by three basis points to 359 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, its index slipped 0.2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Argentina's debt, however, weakened significantly. Its spread widened by 52 basis points to 1045 basis points over Treasurys. In price, its index dove 4%. Investors continue to move out of Argentina assets, after Argentine President Cristina Kirchner said Monday she will ask Congress for approval to expropriate a 51% stake in Argentina's largest oil-and-gas producer, \f28 \uc2 \f2 YPF SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 YPF\f28 \uc2 \f2 , YPFD.BA), from its controlling shareholder, Spain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Repsol YPF SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (REP.MC, REPYY).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com @djfxtrader\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Yeliz Candemir contributed to this article. [ 18-04-12 2032GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120418e84i0016c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
