\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks, Bonds Rise With Global Markets; Merval Up 1.9%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2012\par 22:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's benchmark stock index closed higher for a third straight session Tuesday, led by gains in financial and industrial shares.\par \par \uc2 The Merval index of leading shares rose 1.9% to 2833.23 on volume of 50.4 million pesos ($11.7 million).\par \par \uc2 U.S. and European stock markets, which heavily influence the Merval, closed broadly higher as investors cheered U.S. aluminum maker \uc2 Alcoa Inc\uc2 .'s (AA) results and tuned out Europe's simmering sovereign-debt problems.\par \par \uc2 Brian Joseph, a senior trader at local brokerage Puente, said investors might have gotten a bit ahead of themselves following last week's 12.5% rise in the Merval. Joseph attributed the rally to a pair of U.S. money managers buying shares in banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) and a handful of benchmark bonds.\par \par \uc2 "I'm still afraid of what might happen in Europe. The numbers and the situation [over there] haven't changed," he said.\par \par \uc2 Among local issues, shares of banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) rose nearly 2% to ARS3.65; bank \uc2 Banco Macro SA\uc2  (BMA.BA, BMA) rose 3.2% to ARS11.45; telephone company \uc2 Telecom Argentina SA\uc2  (TEO, TECO2.BA) closed 4.4% at ARS19.00; and steel tube maker \uc2 Tenaris SA\uc2  (TS, TS.BA) rose 2.9% to ARS93.00.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS515.6 million, accounting for 51% of the total volume of securities traded on the exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 The Bonar X rose 0.6% in price terms to close at ARS417.40, yielding 8.36%. The Bogar 2018 closed 2% higher at ARS226.00, to yield 10.74%.\par \par \uc2 The 2033 Discount bond rose 3.2% to ARS130.50, to yield 12.56%. The Boden 2015 rose 0.5% to ARS451.00, yielding 6.34%.\par \par \uc2 The 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrant rose 0.8% to ARS10.9780, while dollar GDP warrants closed 0.1% higher at ARS59.89.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to close at ARS4.3125 to the U.S. dollar on the MAE local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  wholesale market versus ARS4.3135 at Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 Puente said in its afternoon note to clients that the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased about $170 million in U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso from strengthening below the ARS4.31 level as exporters repatriated the proceeds of their sales.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the peso on a gradual weakening trend with a view to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also takes advantage of large dollar inflows to build its international reserves, which totaled $46.25 billion Monday, up from a multi-year low of $44.70 billion on Dec. 14.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 10-01-12 2131GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120110e81a0015v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
